---
description: Optional Mental CLI time tracking. Self-gates on heartbeat track.enabled. Never prompt to enable.
alwaysApply: false
---

If `mental heartbeat --json` includes `data.track.enabled`, follow the Mental Track skill. When tracking is on and `runningCount` is 0 (or the runner cannot continue), call `mental track start --via <host> --json` with short AI-generated internal and customer-ready title/body. Start twice is safe (ensure-running). At park/handoff/journal, regenerate customer copy from the completed outcome on that same command; billable defaults to wall. If JSON includes `review.kind: "customer-copy"`, generate and amend missing copy. Ask only when client identity, billable treatment, or safe wording is genuinely ambiguous. Renderer-safe question = one plain-text draft prompt, 2–3 short single-select `{ id, label }` options, `(Recommended)` in the first label, `allow_multiple: false`; use the host's structured question UI or the same numbered text fallback. If tracking is off, do nothing. Do not enable it without consent this turn. Never invent a start clock or smaller billable duration. Never `git add` `time.sqlite` or an export.
